   "fix": "Rewrite `valenceNumber` as `Pi.single q 1 + Pi.single q' (-1)` (`sub_eq_add_neg`, `\u2190 Pi.single_neg`) and apply `Pi.single_add_single_eq_single_add_single (u := (1 : \u2124)) (v := -1) one_ne_zero (neg_ne_zero.2 one_ne_zero)`; the `u = v` disjunct dies by `(1 : \u2124) \u2260 -1` and the `u + v = 0` disjunct by the `valenceQuark \u2260 valenceAntiquark` hypothesis. This also yields the unconditional iff (pairs agree, or both mesons are unflavoured), making the hypothesis optional. Add `import Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Pi.Lemmas` if not already transitive.",
   "issue": "`valenceNumber_inj` hand-proves a strictly weaker case of Mathlib's `Pi.single_add_single_eq_single_add_single` (additive form of `Pi.mulSingle_mul_mulSingle_eq_mulSingle_mul_mulSingle`), which already characterises when `single k u + single l v = single m u + single n v`.",
